<h3>1. First, a correction — the original text is verifiable</h3>

<p>Thariq&rsquo;s core text is <strong><em>A Field Guide to Fable: Finding Your Unknowns</em></strong>, published on X. Its opening sentence starts from the observation that working with Fable 5 makes him relearn an old lesson. <strong>&ldquo;The map is not the territory.&rdquo;</strong> It means the world the user described in prompts, specs, and documents is not the same as the actual code, data, organization, and user behavior.</p>

